lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346069 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;Arnagara@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="346069" owner_email="mohammed@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/69/346069/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I41bde38ee08a81f731c73fda6485402c10c4b64e" commit="0c2cb08e8d6011138add1dcc0534c3b1e61cf5c3" commit_message="FROMLIST: ath10k: Ensure peer_map references are cleaned up  While debugging OS crashes due to firmware crashes, I enabled kasan, and it noticed that peer objects were being used-after-freed.  Looks like there are two places we could be leaving stale references in the peer-map, so clean that up.  (source: https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/8727821)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49260 TEST=build and tested basic wifi functionality on gale  Change-Id: I41bde38ee08a81f731c73fda6485402c10c4b64e Signed-off-by: Ben Greear &lt;greearb@candelatech.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;arnagara@codeaurora.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Maharaja Kennadyrajan &lt;mkenna@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346070 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ashok Raj Nagarajan &lt;Arnagara@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="346070" owner_email="mohammed@qti.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/70/346070/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="m